			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828012">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The Medicine Man is a sculpture that activates when an individual lowers their guard or gets distracted within the statue's area of effect. The victim is unaware of this, but will see the manifestation of the sculpture's consciousness (as in &quot;its soul&quot;), which calls itself The Medicine Man. Once confronted with the medicine man, said individual will never be able to fully focus/concentrate again (unknowingly), which makes the individual more vulnerable to the sculpture's effect. When exposed to the statue for too long, one could enter a comatose state or develop Alzheimer's.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>When trying to prevent an individual from totally succumbing to the medicine man by attempting to improve their ability to focus with external forces (caffeine, adrenaline injection, etc.), Medicine Man will switch said individual's consciousness with itself, trapping the individual consciousness in the statue. Medicine Man can then host a body until it finds another statue to reside in.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
Medicine Man traveled from sculpture to sculpture, while leaving behind a trail of corrupted minds. This is how the foundation found him.<br />
Inside the foundation, Medicine Man is appreciated for its vast amount of knowledge about chemistry and biology and is sometimes given a host to be interviewed by researchers.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
Opposite of cognitohazard that corrupts the mind without the victim knowing, which I personally find quite creepy</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
I had already started a draft in the sandbox because I didn't know i needed a greenlight.</p>

